<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sangye Gyatso</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1653">1653</a>–<a href="/years/1705">1705</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Desi Sangye Gyatso</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sangye Gyatso was regent, or desi, of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tibet">Tibet</a> from 1679 under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/5th-dalai-lama">Fifth Dalai Lama</a>. He concealed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dalai-lama">Dalai Lama</a>'s death in 1682 for some fifteen years while completing the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/potala-palace">Potala Palace</a>, and wrote major works on medicine, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylonian-astronomy">astronomy</a> and history. His rivalry with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lhazang-khan">Lhazang Khan</a> of the Khoshut ended when Lhazang's forces captured and killed him in 1705.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sangye-gyatso.jpg" alt="Sangye Gyatso" width="320" height="341" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Dieter Schuh · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sangs-rgyas_rgya-mtsho.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
